---

### 1. **Add New Product to Inventory**

```plantuml
@startuml
start
:Enter product details;
:Check if product exists;
if (Product exists?) then (yes)
  :Update inventory;
else (no)
  :Add new product;
endif
:Save to database;
:Send confirmation;
stop
@enduml
```

---

### 2. **Receive New Goods and Update Inventory**

```plantuml
@startuml
start
:Receive goods;
:Verify goods;
:Update inventory;
:Generate purchase record;
:Notify goods receipt;
stop
@enduml
```

---

### 3. **Generate Sales Order and Update Inventory**

```plantuml
@startuml
start
:Customer places order;
:Check stock;
if (Stock available?) then (yes)
  :Update inventory;
  :Generate sales order;
  :Create shipping order;
else (no)
  :Notify stock shortage;
  :Generate backorder;
endif
stop
@enduml
```

---

### 4. **Generate Low Inventory Alert**

```plantuml
@startuml
start
:Check inventory levels;
:Identify low stock items;
if (Low stock?) then (yes)
  :Generate restock alert;
  :Create restock order;
else (no)
  :Continue monitoring;
endif
stop
@enduml
```

---

### 5. **Generate Inventory Report**

```plantuml
@startuml
start
:Select report type;
:Generate and display report;
:Save or export report;
stop
@enduml
```

---

### 6. **Product Return Process**

```plantuml
@startuml
start
:Receive return request;
:Check return eligibility;
if (Eligible?) then (yes)
  :Update inventory;
  :Process refund;
else (no)
  :Reject return;
endif
stop
@enduml
```

---

### 7. **Inventory Audit**

```plantuml
@startuml
start
:Perform inventory audit;
:Compare physical vs system stock;
if (Discrepancy?) then (yes)
  :Adjust inventory;
  :Notify manager;
else (no)
  :Confirm accuracy;
endif
:Generate audit report;
stop
@enduml
```

---

### 8. **System User Operations**

```plantuml
@startuml
start
:Enter login details;
:Validate login;
if (Login successful?) then (yes)
  :Select operation module;
  :Perform actions;
else (no)
  :Show error message;
endif
stop
@enduml
```

